## Codebase
Code lives at the repository root. The language initializer (go mod / uv / npm)
owns the layout and dependencies; jig does not impose one.{{range .Slots}}
- {{.Dir}}/ — {{.Lang}}{{end}}
- Go: build into bin/ (the directory is in .gitignore), e.g.
  go build -o bin/{{.Name}} . — not a bare go build in the module root.

## Working rules
- Show the plan before edits; proceed after confirmation.
- The simple solution for the task at hand, no needless abstraction.
- Product documents go in docs/, never in the code.
- Git: commit messages in English; branches feature/, fix/, docs/.

